{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7976","id":5219129593,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNxWY-Q","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7976","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7976.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7976.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7976","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7976/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7976/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7976/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/3d3b642949af5ce3da1541f5b2ecee5c94966596","number":7976,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(id): id.device.v1 MQTT device bridge spec + labelled PoC (#2343)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #2343.\n\n## What\n\nThe `id.device.v1` MQTT device-bridge **spec plus a labelled PoC**, exactly the remainder scoped by #2343's 2026-11-08 triage. Nothing here is production firmware or a production bridge.\n\n- **`doc/2026-11-09T05-00-00Z_feature_mqtt_device_bridge_id_device_v1/`** — the schema doc: topic table, per-world prefix, one connection per device, example documents for manifest / wants / cap-result / surface / events, wire bounds, and the recorded recommendations (retention, TLS + per-device credentials, reconnect/backoff, device-side journaling, minimum `time.tick`, closed firmware subset).\n- **`pkgs/id/src/device_bridge.rs`** — the PoC module (labelled as such in its module docs): topic helpers, fail-closed `Authenticator`, `Bridge::evaluate_wants` with the web refusal vocabulary, `FakeBroker` (retained manifest, retained-wants ban, wire bounds, auth), `FakeDevice` (journal across reconnects, 1 Hz tick floor, capped exponential backoff, encoder-as-`Key` with a signed delta).\n\nA real MQTT transport replaces `FakeBroker` without touching `Bridge` — that seam is the point of the PoC.\n\n## Decisions reused from #5901 (not reopened)\n\nRetained manifest only · TLS plus per-device credentials · closed device subset (`device.info`, small `screen`/`text`, closed `form.*`, `loc.position` when GNSS present, key/encoder events) · bridge as translator. #2028 still defers production rollout; #5783 owns boards, firmware, OTA and power. Home Assistant interop is recorded as out-of-scope-but-supported.\n\n## Bounds\n\nReuses the host constants rather than restating them: 64 KiB `wants`/events, 8 KiB args. One finding worth noting: oversize args are rejected by `parse_wants` at parse time, before any per-request evaluation — the PoC test asserts that host boundary instead of inventing a per-request code that the host never emits.\n\n## Tests\n\n```\ncargo test --lib device_bridge   # 11 passed\n```\n\nCovering: topic shape, retained manifest for late subscribers, the full manifest→wants→result flow, unknown cap, ungranted cap, retained-wants rejection, oversize wants, oversize args at the host parse boundary, fail-closed auth (wrong token, unknown device, unauthenticated publish), minimum tick, backoff monotonicity/cap, encoder-to-`Key` delta.\n\nNo production code paths are modified: `lib.rs` gains one `pub mod` line.\n\nAgent: `repo-worker-code` · lane `c8b9355e-319a-4640-8096-7ad19480d151` · queue task 13917.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796793574&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7976&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7976&signature=f9a4ea077c47d2725d7fe1f022bc606eca04ce18dea38ebb6dfe965380692a71\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7976?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T05:19:31Z","updated_at":"2026-11-14T21:51:43Z","closed_at":"2026-11-14T21:51:23Z","merged_at":"2026-11-14T21:51:23Z","merge_commit_sha":"1fd1a80b69a7a01e5609aad848e229c6033c6bed","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https: